body:
Well the DateTime test certainly does work on 32 bit systems. 

``` php
echo 'PHP Int Size = ' . PHP_INT_SIZE  . "<br>";
$time = DateTime::createFromFormat('Y-m-d', '2048-12-17');
// or $time = new DateTime('2048-12-17');
echo '2048-12-17 is parsed = ' . $time->format('d-M-Y');
```

The above code for 32 bit system returns:

```
PHP Int Size = 4
2048-12-17 is parsed = 17-Dec-2048
```

Will need to test other part of the code.
